  676:     /***************************************************************************
  677:     * The wake count defines the number of Bus Clock cycles it takes for the
  678:     * flash or EEPROM to wake up from a low power mode independent of the chip
  679:     * power mode. Wake up time for these blocks is 5 us.
  680:     * The granularity of this register is 2 Bus Clock cycles, so a value of 0x1E
  681:     * (30d) defines the wake up time as 60 cycles of the Bus Clock.
  682:     * This register needs to be written with a value dependent on the Bus Clock
  683:     * frequency so that the duration of the cycles is equal to or greater than
